<title>FRANCE: U.N. approves more France-Iraq sugar deals.</title>
<headline>U.N. approves more France-Iraq sugar deals.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Nations has now approved the sale of around 80,000 tonnes of French sugar to Iraq under a U.N. monitored oil-for-food pact, a French government source said on Monday.</p>
<p>The source also said that France had not asked the U.N. to clear additional sugar sales.</p>
<p>&quot;To this date everything has been cleared. There are no more approvals pending,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The last count on March 24 showed the total at 50,000 tonnes of sugar.</p>
</text>
